1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,568
听：Before Clicking Agree.

2
00:00:02,568 --> 00:00:05,136
跟读：Before Clicking Agree.

3
00:00:05,136 --> 00:00:30,024
听：Omar downloaded an app that promised to organise his study notes. Before he could use it, a message requested consent to collect personal data. The document was long, and he nearly accepted it without reading. Then he noticed that the app wanted access to his location even when it was closed.

4
00:00:30,024 --> 00:00:54,912
跟读：Omar downloaded an app that promised to organise his study notes. Before he could use it, a message requested consent to collect personal data. The document was long, and he nearly accepted it without reading. Then he noticed that the app wanted access to his location even when it was closed.

5
00:00:54,912 --> 00:01:20,832
听：Omar asked his sister, who studies computing, whether this permission was necessary. She explained that an algorithm could use several small details to build a profile. She did not claim that every app was dangerous. Instead, she encouraged him to check the purpose of each request and the company's privacy policy.

6
00:01:20,832 --> 00:01:46,752
跟读：Omar asked his sister, who studies computing, whether this permission was necessary. She explained that an algorithm could use several small details to build a profile. She did not claim that every app was dangerous. Instead, she encouraged him to check the purpose of each request and the company's privacy policy.

7
00:01:46,752 --> 00:02:13,224
听：The company said that it stored information securely. Omar wanted to know how long the records would be retained and whether users could delete them. Strong encryption might reduce some risks, but it would not explain why unnecessary information was collected. A security claim needed evidence, not just an attractive label.

8
00:02:13,224 --> 00:02:39,696
跟读：The company said that it stored information securely. Omar wanted to know how long the records would be retained and whether users could delete them. Strong encryption might reduce some risks, but it would not explain why unnecessary information was collected. A security claim needed evidence, not just an attractive label.

9
00:02:39,696 --> 00:03:04,392
听：Omar eventually chose a version with fewer permissions. He also disabled notifications during study time. The decision did not make him an expert, but it gave him more control. He learned to ask a practical question: does the convenience justify the information I am being asked to share?

10
